message: "If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata below."
title: "CurvatureDistinguishability.jl"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Gogîță"
    given-names: "Paul-Adrian"
version: "1.0.0"
date-released: "2026-09-22"
repository-code: "https://github.com/PaulGoG/CurvatureDistinguishability.jl"
license: MIT
abstract: >-
  Computational proof of the quartic distinguishability law for
  space-based gravitational-wave interferometry: the squared distance
  between a two-source signal and the best-fit single-source template
  scales as D² ≈ (1/16) K(u) δ⁴, governed by the extrinsic curvature K(u)
  of the signal manifold. The package provides the waveform and detector
  model, the differential-geometry engine, box-constrained inference on
  CPU and GPU backends, validated configuration with provenance-stamped
  runs, and publication plotting.
keywords:
  - gravitational waves
  - LISA
  - source confusion
  - signal manifold
  - extrinsic curvature
  - Julia
